    "['isis ipv6 enable [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols isis interface <interface-name> ipv6-adjacency-segment', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the Juniper equivalent of the HUAWEI command `isis ipv6 enable 1`:\\n\\n##\\nset protocols isis interface <interface-name> ipv6-adjacency-segment\\n##\\n\\nNote: \\n1. In Juniper, you need to specify the interface name (replacing `<interface-name>` with the actual interface, e.g., `ge-1/0/1.0` or `lo0.0`)\\n2. The `1` in HUAWEI's command refers to the IS-IS process ID, which in Juniper is implicitly handled since Juniper typically uses a single IS-IS instance\\n3. The Juniper command enables IS-IS for IPv6 on the specified interface, including IPv6 adjacency formation and IPv6 routing\", 'trans_template': 'set protocols isis interface <interface-name> ipv6-adjacency-segment'}]]": 1,
